invariant: INV-16
file: src/rsa_sign64_blind.h
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: blinded_prime_exponent multiplies r by p in place of p - 1, so
  each half walks d + r p, whose power is m^(d + r) mod p and not m^d.
  The signature fails its check, and bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test finds the
  64-bit signer refusing its own signature.

--- old
    p_words[0] &= ~(uint64_t)1;
--- new
    p_words[0] &= ~(uint64_t)0;
